s://api.github.com/users/ncullen93/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncullen93/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncullen93/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ncullen93/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-02-23T04:32:04Z","updated_at":"2017-02-23T05:09:35Z","body":"I am getting this error.. Is there any way to get around this without root privledges? chown and chmod don't seem to help.\r\n\r\nI've tried on just about every version of bazel with the same results..Using centOS, tried a bunch of different versions of gcc, tried java 7 and 8..  \r\nAlways ending in:\r\n```\r\n## Build informations\r\n   - [Build log](http://ci.bazel.io/job/Bazel/JAVA_VERSION=1.8,PLATFORM_NAME=linux-x86_64/1246/)\r\n   - [Commit](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/commit/80a07b5)\r\nUncompressing......\r\n/home/anthill/ncullen/.bazelrc already exists, moving it to /home/anthill/ncullen/.bazelrc.bak.\r\nINFO: Reading 'startup' options from .bazelrc: --batch\r\nWarning: ignoring LD_PRELOAD in environment.\r\nError: mkdir('/home/anthill/ncullen/.cache/bazel/_bazel_ncullen'): Permission denied\r\n```\r\nI've tried from both the source code running `./compile.sh` and the installer running e.g `./bazel-0.2.0-installer-linux-x86_64.sh --user`..\r\n\r\nI'm using the following bazelrc file.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /tmp\r\ncat >/tmp/bazelrc <<EOF\r\nstartup --batch\r\nbuild --spawn_strategy=standalone --genrule_strategy=standalone\r\nEOF\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/281891981/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ncullen93","id":13004360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMDA0MzYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13004360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url"